Overview
--------
The "Setup Plugin" can be used to setup all or most configuration parameters 
of VDR distributions via the OSD.

The Plugin can be easily configured by editing the following XML-Files:

  [PLUGINS-CONFIG-DIR]/setup/vdr-setup.xml
  [PLUGINS-CONFIG-DIR]/setup/vdr-menu.xml

Both files can also be language specific, e.g. vdr-setup.de_DE.xml
(OSDLanguage from setup.conf).

vdr-setup.xml
=============
Holds the Setup configuration, see MANUAL.DE.

vdr-menu.xml
============
Holds the VDR Menu-Submenu configuration, see MANUAL.DE.

The example files of the original plugin are not included.

Help files should be placed in [PLUGINS-CONFIG-DIR]/setup/help

Requirements
============
VDR >= 2.8. The plugin builds against an unpatched VDR. The VDR source
directory is needed at build time, because the setup classes are extracted
from its menu.c (set VDRSRC if it is not ../../..).

The main menu of an unpatched VDR does not use vdr-menu.xml. "Menu Edit"
only changes the main menu, if VDR is patched with
patches/vdr-2.8.4-setup.diff:

  cd vdr-2.8.4
  patch -p1 < PLUGINS/src/setup/patches/vdr-2.8.4-setup.diff

The patch adds submenu and tinyxml to VDR and defines USE_SETUP
(build VDR with SETUP=0 to disable it). VDR then loads
[PLUGINS-CONFIG-DIR]/setup/vdr-menu.<OSDLanguage>.xml or vdr-menu.xml
when the main menu is opened. If neither exists, the standard main menu
is shown.


Also please make sure, that the file specified with the parameter "sysconfigFile"
 (see vdr-setup.xml) exists.
The Plugin will save the configured parameters in this file in the form of:

VARIABLE="value"
...

The sysconfig file can be just included by any Shell-Scripts which may interpret 
the stored Variables.


All Variable names can be specified within the vdr-setup.xml configuration file
itself. The predefined Variable PLUGINLIST will hold all activated Plugins including
their optional parameters, and can be used in the VDR startup script to dynamically
specify the Plugins.


Detailed Information currently only available in german language.
see MANUAL.DE and http://www.vdrtools.de




